>>
endobj
1213 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Dumbell Exercises - Exercises such as the Dumbell Shoulder Press and Incline Dumbbell Bench Press can be replaced by Barbell variations of those exercises. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
1214 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Assisted Pull Up Machine - The first point of call would be to use a heavy resistance band. Use a step or box to give yourself the height required to step into the band, this will help you to do pull ups. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
1215 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (However if this is too challenging, using a bar in a squat rack, set at chest height, can allow you to do Floor assisted Pull Ups where your buttocks and feet touch the floor with your knees bent at the start of every repetition. You can produce the same motion as a pull up. Finally, simply using a bench, a box or another stable raised surface underneath a pull up bar can help you to do Pull Ups. Keep your legs on the raised surface and use them to help you do the pull up by straightening your legs on the way up, and bending your knees on the way down. Select the option that works best for your skill level. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
1216 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Rear Delt Machine - The Dumbell Rear Delt Fly can be used as a replacement for this machine. I find the machine smoother and allows me to push to a greater intensity than dumbells, so to match this without the machine I would use a Superset of Rear Delt Dumbell Flys \(15 reps\) straight into Resistance Band Face Pulls \(15 reps\). This is a solid alternative to work your Rear Delts. )
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1217 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Lateral Pulldown - Hooking a resistance band to a surface above can act as a Lateral Pulldown. Simply doing a Band Pull Apart with a resistance band starting from over your head can also act as a Lateral Pulldown.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1218 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 287 0 R
/E (Triceps Pushdown / Triceps Behind The Head Extension - Instead of Cables, Resistance Bands attached to an overhead surface such as bar or Squat Rack, make for an excellent alternative for these exercises.)
/Pg 61 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
