2755 0 obj
<<
/Title (You have now completed a year of training.  In your second and third year, I want you to apply all the 12 techniques you have learned in each month together in your workouts.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2103 0 R
/Next 3100 0 R
>>
endobj
2756 0 obj
<<
/Title (In your second and third years, if cardio starts to get boring, consider learning a skill like boxing for cardio, doing exercise classes or doing Youtube workouts. We will move on to some variations of cardio workouts to improve your body and build you up to train like an athlete instead of doing casual cardio.)
/Dest [62 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2103 0 R
/Prev 3101 0 R
>>
endobj
2757 0 obj
<<
/Title (They reach a level where they have a knowledge in their head of multiple ways to workout and push themselves. Because to improve in the gym, there is always a personal record to be found every session.  How you improve is to always find that personal record each and every time you enter the gym. It can be as simple as doing 1 more repetition than last week on an exercise.)
/Dest [63 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1305 0 R
/Prev 2104 0 R
/Next 3102 0 R
>>
endobj
2758 0 obj
<<
/Title (Theres always a PR \(Personal Record\) to hit, but you need to be in the gym to hit it, enjoying yourself, and being able to know the options available to you based on different situations. It is important to have knowledge so you can find what you love in fitness, and awareness of when to make a change. Some people may love just one sport and style of workout their whole life, and others need variety. Some people get injured doing one style of workout for too long and need to make substitutions or slight programme changes to stay active .)
/Dest [63 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1305 0 R
/Prev 3103 0 R
/Next 2105 0 R
>>
endobj
