3750 0 obj
<<
/Title (Post-exhaustion is the reverse of pre-exhaustion. You hit the compound movement first to recruit maximum muscle fibres, then immediately follow it with an isolation exercise to finish off the target muscle completely. For example, leg press followed immediately by leg extensions ensures the quads are fully worked even after the glutes and hamstrings have taken some of the load in the compound. This month, look out for exercise pairs marked \(POST-EXHAUST\) and move between them with zero rest.)
/Dest [42 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3733 0 R
/First 3769 0 R
/Last 3770 0 R
/Count -2
>>
endobj
